  "findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Exact complete-string alphabet",
      "conclusion": "The existing K identity fullmatch runs first. The second fullmatch adds exactly FF01..FF5E (94 scalars), 3000, 2011 and 2026, and admits no others. No prefix or per-character partial fast path is used."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Fixed mapping",
      "conclusion": "All 97 table keys are explicit and disjoint: fullwidth ASCII maps by codepoint minus FEE0; 3000 maps to 0020, 2011 to 2010, and 2026 to three 002E. Each target is inside K's certified identity alphabet. Unknown characters cannot be silently left unchanged by translate because fullmatch precedes it."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Whole-string normalization proof",
      "conclusion": "The eligible alphabet consists of K's identity alphabet plus only these mappings. Their compatibility decompositions have the exact registered targets. Those targets are ASCII, the admitted CJK ranges or admitted punctuation; they contain no marks, Hangul Jamo or other admitted second composition operands. Thus decomposition cannot reorder or compose across these admitted boundaries. The target alphabet is closed under the existing Camel insertion of ASCII spaces and casefold. The old post-casefold NFKD and Mn removal are identities on this path."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Semantic operation order",
      "conclusion": "translate executes once before the unchanged CamelCase substitution and casefold. alphaＢeta therefore becomes alphaBeta before the historical lowercase-to-uppercase split, preserving ['alpha', 'beta']. Existing ASCII and K identity paths never translate."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Fallback and hooks",
      "conclusion": "The initial text.isascii truth is still consumed once. Exact str type, existing supported UCD version, and identity of normalize/category/Camel/strip functions gate both certificates. Subclasses, unknown versions, modified hooks and all characters outside the full alphabet retain the literal historical normalization order. No broader promise is made for mutation of private certificate constants."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Unchanged downstream behavior",
      "conclusion": "The Camel statement through the end of text.py is byte-identical to K. Extraction offsets, source mapping, segmentation, token budgets, candidate construction, caches, persistence and interfaces are unchanged by this candidate."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Artificial fixture adequacy",
      "conclusion": "The 14 new methods enumerate the full Unicode codepoint membership of the extended alphabet, all 97 mappings and their targets, whole-alphabet closure, representative ordered boundaries, literal terms/query/index parity, deterministic invented mixtures, excluded composition cases, actual C-call counts, hook/subclass fallback, real SQLite FTS and complete native/token/title-follow payload equality. The literal historical comparator patches lexical.terms, store.terms and token_budget.terms so all shipping bindings use the same reference."
    }
